The rate-limit test in auth.spec.ts uses the same API — my new implementation preserves semantics (fixed window, count-based). Test should still pass.

Now add the watchdog to the smoke script. And also — one important thing: the rate-limit test in the smoke script... the smoke script's rate limit section: it emits [HTTP] lines... the smoke script tests rate limiting via HTTP: registers 3 accounts → 4th 429. With the new implementation this works the same.

Add watchdog to smoke-staging.mjs:
```js
const WATCHDOG = setTimeout(() => {
  console.error(`[WATCHDOG] smoke test exceeded 4 minutes — aborting. Last known requests logged above.`);
  process.exit(1);
}, 4 * 60 * 1000);
```
And clear it before exit... actually if main() completes, clearTimeout(WATCHDOG) then process.exit with the summary. The watchdog must fire DURING hangs — setTimeout keeps the event loop alive, and when it fires → prints → exit(1) ✓.

